course: dictionary
lesson: 7370
title: The Pleiades, the Seven Sisters
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The Pleiades is a proper noun. It is the name of one particular group of stars, so it starts with a capital letter. A cluster is a group of things close together. «Stars born from the same cloud often stay together for a while as a cluster, like the Pleiades.»
explain: The sentence gives you clues. The Pleiades is about 440 light years away and about 100 million years old. It is very far away and very old, yet we can still see it in the night sky. Its other name, the Seven Sisters, tells you how many bright stars people often count.
explain: Different people have different names for the same stars. In Japan it is called Subaru, and Māori in New Zealand call it Matariki. The names change from place to place, but they all point to the same cluster in the sky.
fact: The Pleiades is a bright cluster of stars in the constellation Taurus.
fact: The Pleiades is also called the Seven Sisters.
fact: In Greek myths, the Pleiades were seven sisters, daughters of Atlas, who were turned into stars.
fact: You can see the Pleiades without a telescope in winter in the north, and people with good eyes count six or seven stars.
fact: In New Zealand, Matariki marks the Māori New Year and is a public holiday.
exercise: «Stars born from the same cloud often stay together as a cluster, like the Pleiades.» What is a cluster? | A single star far away | A dark cloud with no stars | *A group of things close together | A very large telescope
exercise: «Taurus has the V-shaped Hyades and the Pleiades, and Gemini has the twin stars Castor and Pollux.» Which constellation is the Pleiades in? | Gemini | Ursa Major | Cassiopeia | *Taurus
exercise: Ana reads that Matariki marks a special day in New Zealand. What does Matariki mark? | *The Māori New Year | A new bike race | A school holiday for the stars | The first day of summer in Japan
test: Japan calls the Pleiades Subaru. What other name do people use for the Pleiades? | *The Seven Sisters | The Milky Way | The Big Dipper | Polaris
test: Why does the word Pleiades start with a capital letter? | *Because it is the name of one particular cluster of stars | Because it is a long word | Because it is very bright | Because it starts a sentence in every book
exam: In Greek myths, who were the Pleiades? | Seven dogs who chased Orion across the sky | Seven kings who ruled Taurus | Seven brothers who guarded the sea | *Seven sisters, daughters of Atlas, who were turned into stars
